CHEMTRAIN-DEPLOY examples
=========================

in.chemtrain-deploy evaluates two noninteracting Lennard-Jones clusters with
two and three particles. The example compares the energy and every
pressure-tensor component with the smoothly truncated LAMMPS
``lj/charmm/coul/charmm`` reference. The comparison checks neighbor
completeness, the switching region, and the strain-derived virial. The default
uses ``lennard_jones_sparse.ptb`` with Newton pair forces enabled. Run both
graph representations with Newton pair on and off::

  lmp -in in.chemtrain-deploy -var model lennard_jones_sparse.ptb -var newton_pair on
  lmp -in in.chemtrain-deploy -var model lennard_jones_sparse.ptb -var newton_pair off
  lmp -in in.chemtrain-deploy -var model lennard_jones_dense.ptb -var newton_pair on
  lmp -in in.chemtrain-deploy -var model lennard_jones_dense.ptb -var newton_pair off

in.chemtrain-deploy-bulk runs a periodic FCC Lennard-Jones system for 20 NVE
steps, writes potential, kinetic, and total energy to ``energy-bulk.dat``, and
checks the maximum total-energy drift per atom during the run. The bulk example
accepts the same ``model`` and ``newton_pair`` variables.

The fixtures use LAMMPS ``lj`` units with epsilon, sigma, and mass set to one.
The energy is smoothly truncated from an onset of 2.0 to a cutoff of 2.5. The
format 5 bundles contain separate Newton-on and Newton-off executables. The
package requires a LAMMPS executable configured with CHEMTRAIN-DEPLOY. The
cluster reference also requires the MOLECULE package. CUDA is currently the
only backend covered by end-to-end tests.

The fixtures are generated by
``examples/chemtrain-deploy/export_lennard_jones.py`` in the chemtrain source
tree. The export script uses a direct JAX implementation of the smoothly
truncated 12-6 potential, exports one bundle with CPU and CUDA implementations
per neighbor format, and does not depend on JAX-MD potential helpers.
Regenerate the files from the chemtrain repository root with::

  python examples/chemtrain-deploy/export_lennard_jones.py \
    /path/to/lammps/examples/PACKAGES/chemtrain-deploy

Fixture provenance and SHA-256:

* ``lennard_jones_dense.ptb``:
  ``a1880c91380457cb12137c9da99f2ae0ce911e4e9facb297e13403045e087273``
* ``lennard_jones_sparse.ptb``:
  ``eb31fd1a0663eb590eb3e1193cc66948397a5714cacffbd09088411348bd90de``
